"enhance_help" = "How to test whisper boost…";
"enhance_instructions" = "1. Enable boost\nChoose a physical mic in this app. Turning on “Boost quiet speech” automatically enables keep-alive. Start at +12 dB.\n\n2. Set up your dictation app\nChoose BlackHole 2ch as its microphone. If it has no device selector, change the system input to BlackHole instead; leave boost enabled with the original mic selected here. Keep music output unchanged.\n\n3. Compare results\nRead the same sentence at the same volume using the physical mic and then BlackHole. Reduce gain if noise is too loud; increase it if speech is still too quiet. For an A/B test, keep BlackHole and the same gain selected. Try “Gentle denoise”, then “Voice clarity”. Denoise reduces steady noise; clarity cuts rumble and gently emphasizes speech. If quiet word endings disappear or hiss gets stronger, turn that option off. These are local filters, not AI speech separation; recognition gains need testing.\n\n4. Finish\nSwitch your dictation app (and system input, if changed) back to the physical mic before turning boost off. Turning boost off preserves keep-alive; turning keep-alive off disables both. Turning boost off or quitting stops this app’s audio to BlackHole.\n\nAfter a normal relaunch, boost and both filters are off; gain resets to +12 dB. In-app updates resume your current audio settings. No audio is saved or uploaded. AirPods capture may still affect music quality.";
